summary:
- topic: Student Recognition
  text: The board celebrated the AA State Champion Girls Basketball Team and recognized
    Scholastic Art Award Winners, highlighting student achievements in both athletics
    and the arts.
- topic: FY2026 Budget Presentation
  text: Superintendent Angela Atkinson Duina presented the proposed FY26 budget, emphasizing
    the difficult financial situation driven by declining enrollment, increased needs
    of diverse student populations (special education, multilingual), and the depletion
    of federal carryover funds. The budget aims to balance taxpayer concerns with
    student needs.
- topic: Proposed Staff Reductions
  text: The budget includes significant staff reductions across the district office,
    various school-based teaching positions (ESOL, SEL, social worker, classroom teachers,
    specialists, technology integrators), and educational technicians (library, ESOL,
    special roles). All affected ed techs have been offered alternative positions
    within the district.
- topic: Curriculum Leadership Reorganization
  text: To address the elimination of the Director of Curriculum, Instruction, and
    Assessment position, a new curriculum leadership team will be formed, involving
    existing principals and assistant principals, and a redefined Assistant Principal
    for Teaching and Learning role at SOUTH PORTLAND HIGH SCHOOL.
- topic: Community and Staff Concerns
  text: Numerous community members and staff voiced strong concerns about the budget
    process, perceived lack of transparency, and the potential negative impact of
    cuts on critical student services like Social Emotional Learning, ESOL, special
    education, music, and social studies. Many expressed anxiety and disappointment
    over the notification process for affected employees.
- topic: Financial Strategy and Fund Balance
  text: The Superintendent recommended using $800,000 from the district's fund balance
    (savings account) to offset tax increases and save positions, acknowledging the
    need to rebuild this balance in future years. Board members and citizens raised
    questions about long-term financial stability and alternative revenue streams.
- topic: Policy and Program Approvals
  text: The board unanimously approved several policies related to copyright compliance
    and field trips, as well as a pre-kindergarten expansion program through partnerships,
    which was noted to have no direct cost to taxpayers.
